2026-04-26. Follow-on bugfix amendment that aligns the
clause-(h) implementation with the AC text already locked
in amendment #54. Three #54 ACs the build did not actually
satisfy are closed here:

  - **AC.HFX.1 ↔ AC.H.5** — every clause-(h) execution writes
    the audit YAML, regardless of clean-pass / BudgetExhausted
    / ResolverFailure terminus. Pre-amendment, only the three
    error termini wrote the audit; a clean pass produced no
    on-disk artefact.
  - **AC.HFX.2 ↔ AC.H.8** — every clause-(h) execution writes
    `<workspace>/.pos/upgrade/state.yaml`; the next
    invocation auto-discovers prior state and resumes without
    requiring `--conflicts-from`. Pre-amendment, no code path
    wrote state.yaml; idempotency required manual operator
    threading of the prior conflicts YAML.
  - **AC.HFX.3 ↔ AC.H.5 / plan §2 path text** — clause-(h)
    audit lands at `<workspace>/.pos/upgrade/<tag>/audit.yaml`,
    not the global `~/.pos/framework/history/<tag>-conflicts.yaml`.
    Legacy `--staging-dir` (no clause-(h)) keeps writing to
    `paths.conflicts_yaml(tag)` per Hard Constraint 5
    backward-compat.

